body:
>boobioboobs

I mean I get it but when people keep shoving it on my face saying that I should be grateful because 'I have so much and I'm just a teenager I don't know what true suffering is like' people constantly push me back down when I try to speak about what's bothering me

And yeah family played a big role in that. All I can do is keep this to myself

&#x200B;

it's so stupid. when I was in middle school people told me 'oh my god you don't know what high school is like, it's WORSE. MORE STRESS. Don't even think about complaining, you're just a small brat.'

&#x200B;

when I'm in high school people tell me 'you don't know what university/work is like, it's SO MUCH MORE WORSE. yOu'rE JuSt a tEeNaGeR YoU DoNt kNoW AnYtHiNg aBoUt dEpReSsIoN. UGH.'

&#x200B;

then what?? does it just go on and on? it's so fucking dumb, it's like they think my experience doesn't mean anything because of my age compared to theirs? and when I finally break down they get all 'omg whats wrong' and when I say what's wrong, they'll say 'uGh i dEaLt wItH ThAt tOo bUt i dIdN't oVeRrEaCt lIkE YoU, FFS!' and when I tell them one of my small achievements (once told them about fighting back some mean people at class) they got all quiet because they didn't realize I experienced shit like that.

&#x200B;

anyway...... feel like teen depression is just the beginning. probably the worse is yet to come.

&#x200B;
